--- A.3 Code audit (process::exit on resource-holding paths) ---
src/main.rs process::exit occurrences:
  line 73: --help → process::exit(0)  [NON-resource-holding: before any provider acquire]
  line 78: bad arg → process::exit(2) [NON-resource-holding: before any provider acquire]
NO process::exit on resource-holding paths. Cleanup via RAII Drop:
  - DrmProvider::Drop (drm_backend.rs:410) → release() → release_master_lock()
  - SimDisplayProvider::Drop → drops Card (releases master + fd)
  - SimInputProvider::Drop (sim_input.rs:191) → dev_destroy()
  - main() returns Result; catch_unwind → Err("engine panicked") → exit 1

W2 — panic path:
  main.rs:140,211: panic::catch_unwind(AssertUnwindSafe(|| real_main(...)))
  On panic: (1) panic hook fires first (lifecycle.rs:80-97: logs backtrace +
    run_panic_cleanup), (2) catch_unwind catches, (3) main matches Err(_) =>
    Err("engine panicked".into()) → Rust runtime exits 1.
  ACTUAL exit code for panic path = 1 (NOT std 101, because catch_unwind
  catches before the runtime's default abort). ADR-025 §2 table line 49
  maps "engine panic (Err(_))" → exit 1 — UNAMBIGUOUS.